          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 13:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let us plot the points (– 3, 6), (– 2, 4), (0, 0), (1, – 2), (2, – 4), (3, – 6) in the coordinate plane on a graph paper as shown in Fig. 2.7. Join the points (– 3, 6) and (3, – 6) using a ruler. Doing so, observe that all five points lie on a straight line. Can you guess the equation of this line by looking at the relationship between the x and y coordinates of each point?"
            }
          ]
        },
